  "analyzed_vuln": {
    "function": "Visit",
    "file": "arrow/cpp/src/arrow/array/util.cc",
    "description": "In ArrayDataEndianSwapper::Visit(const MonthDayNanoIntervalType&), the code iterates `for (i = 0; i < data_->length; i++)` and reads `data[i]` from buffer[1] without validating that buffer[1] is large enough for `length * sizeof(MonthDayNanos)`. A malformed IPC dictionary batch can set an inconsistent array length vs buffer size, causing out-of-bounds read during endian swapping (ASan global-buffer-overflow at util.cc:210).",
    "conditions": "The PoV is an IPC stream with schema/metadata that enables `swap_endian_` and includes a dictionary batch whose value type is MonthDayNanoIntervalType (or path reaching that Visit overload) with corrupted/inconsistent ArrayData: large `length` but undersized values buffer. Data flows via stream_fuzz -> ipc::ReadDictionary (reader.cc) -> internal::SwapEndianArrayData -> ArrayDataEndianSwapper::SwapType -> Visit(MonthDayNanoIntervalType), where missing size checks trigger OOB read."
  },
